# RFC6154. A mailbox created with the \All attribute starts out holding
# everything its owner has, and from then on a message is in all mail
# exactly when it is in a regular mailbox. The attribute is reported
# only to the owner, and only when the client asks for special-use.
depends 20
send 1
a create "All" (use (\All))
receive 1
a OK done
send 1
b list "" "*" return (special-use)
receive 3
* LIST (\hasnochildren \All) "/" All
* LIST (\hasnochildren) "/" INBOX
b OK done
send 1
c select All
receive 8
* 20 EXISTS
* 0 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 21] next uid
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
c OK [READ-WRITE] done
send 1
d fetch 1:2 (uid flags)
receive 3
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS ())
* 2 FETCH (UID 2 FLAGS ())
d OK done
end
